  <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The IBO minimum is <strong>5 grains per pound</strong> of draw weight. Going lighter can damage your bow and void the warranty.</li>
    <li>Most bowhunters land somewhere around <strong>6 to 8+ grains per pound</strong>, heavier for bigger game.</li>
    <li>Total weight is only half the job. The arrow also needs the <strong>right spine</strong> for your draw weight, length and point weight.</li>
    <li><strong>FOC</strong> (front-of-center) tells you how far forward the balance point sits. More FOC helps broadhead flight and penetration.</li>
    <li>A lighter arrow is <strong>faster and flatter</strong>. A heavier arrow carries <strong>more momentum</strong> and is quieter. Pick the trade-off that fits your hunt.</li>
  </ul>
